\tr{\td{reachability}\td{2.84, 3.00, 2.96 / 27.9}\td{2.30, 2.63, 2.55 / 21.9}\td{2.50, 2.50, 2.42 / 20.7}\td{2.39, 2.32, 2.53 / 20.6}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{2.61, 2.61, 2.82 / 37.5}\td{2.60, 2.74, 2.83 / 37.5}\td{2.48, 2.73, 2.60 / 37.3}\td{2.46, 2.75, 2.63 / 37.2}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{6.44, 6.70, 6.49 / 90.1}\td{6.78, 6.88, 6.86 / 90.2}\td{6.22, 6.90, 6.87 / 89.4}\td{6.28, 6.84, 6.80 / 89.3}}
\tr{\td{Std}\td{11.67, 12.53, 11.50 / 154.9}\td{11.91, 12.32, 11.49 / 155.3}\td{12.50, 12.33, 11.57 / 154.1}\td{12.76, 11.39, 12.44 / 153.9}}
}

\p{reachability also: host depth 512 2.41, 2.39 s and 2048 2.57, 2.37 s (20.7 G both: no CPU difference established); \code{\verb~|lazyeval~} on top 2.24, 2.33 s (20.7 G); v0 8.95, 8.61 s (58.3 G); the reference engine 13.15, 12.78 s. So reachability: -16 \% CPU / -26 \% instructions with \code{\verb~|k2,m3a~} (median 2.96 -> 2.50 s; 0.28x of v0 in the same batch); \code{\verb~|m3a~} is worth -0.5 \% .. -0.9 \% of the instructions on Init, Std and the Cedar slice and -5 \% on reachability. \strong{Init is the open point}: its three \code{\verb~|k2~} rows are 5 \% above its three base rows in CPU (worker CPU 5.97 - 6.04 s against 5.65 - 5.73 s) at +0.1 \% instructions and equal ticks; batch 2 had shown no difference (7.16, 6.85 against 7.13, 6.80). Not resolved under this load. To make the question moot, K2 was then ARMED PER DECLARATION (published 16:06Z): nothing of it runs (no count, no table probe, no firing) until the current declaration has run 16,384 ticks, which no light declaration reaches; an interleaved batch (base, \code{\verb~|k2,m3a~}, 4 pairs per corpus, \code{\verb~|work/m3/batch4.sh~}) is queued behind the measurement lock.}

\p{\strong{After M7's publication of 15:10Z} (case trees that inline the matchers they call; reachability with \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~} fell from 29.3 G to 17.8 G instructions, 16.5 M to 10.1 M ticks) the K2 of 15:05Z was a LOSS on reachability: it fired its own rule where the new tree is better (JVM counters, main tree of 16:10Z: \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~} 10.10 M ticks / 5.55 M records, with \code{\verb~|k2~} 13.22 M / 7.04 M). Published 16:26Z: \strong{a head that has a K1 case tree gets no rule} (the tree is asked for when the head becomes hot). Counters on the main tree of 16:20Z (JVM launcher; \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~} against \code{\verb~|code,casetrees,k2,m3a~}; ticks M / records M / run words M):}

\table{
\tr{\th{workload}\th{\code{\verb~|code,casetrees~}}\th{+ \code{\verb~|k2,m3a~}}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{10.10 / 5.55 / 27.1}\td{9.06 / 5.32 / 25.8 (183 k firings)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|perf/magma-list-deep-n36~}}\td{56.9 / 10.27 / 73.5}\td{7.24 / 1.10 / 7.2 (3.40 M firings)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|perf/magma-list-pair-n21~}}\td{20.9 / 13.64 / 81.2}\td{13.1 / 9.35 / 52.2 (1.22 M firings)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|perf/ite-taken-branch~}}\td{11.2 / 6.70 / 39.6}\td{6.37 / 4.44 / 23.5 (0.42 M firings)}}
}

\p{The final native image (\code{\verb~|work/m3/dist-k2r~} = the published state of 16:26Z), host survey, one run each at load 40 - 60 (CPU s = user + sys; base = \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,probes,code,casetrees~} at 4 MiB -> + \code{\verb~|k2,m3a~}): \code{\verb~|magma-list-deep-n36~} 12.57 -> \strong{1.42 s} (RSS 1603 -> 166 MiB), \code{\verb~|magma-list-pair-n21~} 8.73 -> 5.31 s, \code{\verb~|ite-taken-branch~} 4.04 -> 2.09 s, \code{\verb~|unfold-before-literal~} 6.92 -> 4.31 s (\code{\verb~|m3a~} with M7's threshold 1), \code{\verb~|short-circuit-and~} 3.47 -> 3.59 s, \code{\verb~|gf3-matrix-product~} 2.59 -> 2.40 s. reachability on the host is not resolved (four alternating runs per set: base 1.90 - 3.11 s, \code{\verb~|k2,m3a~} 2.41 - 3.04 s; its counters are 9.83 M -> 8.79 M ticks, 5.02 M -> 4.79 M records, RSS 298 -> 234 MiB): the locked batch 4 above decides.}

\p{\strong{Locked batch 4} (\code{\verb~|work/m3/batch4.out~}, rows \code{\verb~|b4-*~}; the published state of 16:26Z = \code{\verb~|work/m3/dist-k2r~}, native \code{\verb~|-O3~}, container, one worker, base and \code{\verb~|k2,m3a~} INTERLEAVED, 3 pairs per corpus, host load 45 - 52; CPU s of the three runs / instructions G / RSS MiB; base = \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,probes,code,casetrees~} at 4 MiB):}

\table{
\tr{\th{corpus}\th{base}\th{+ \code{\verb~|k2,m3a~}}\th{median CPU}\th{instructions}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{1.46, 1.49, 1.55 / 17.4 / 292}\td{1.38, 1.47, 1.42 / 15.9 / 228}\td{1.49 -> \strong{1.42 s} (-4.7 \%)}\td{-8.6 \%}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice}\td{2.59, 2.52, 2.48 / 38.6 / 182}\td{2.57, 2.47, 2.48 / 38.4 / 182}\td{2.52 -> 2.48 s (-1.6 \%)}\td{-0.5 \%}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{6.11, 5.97, 6.12 / 96.9 / 212}\td{6.07, 6.07, 6.04 / 95.8 / 213}\td{6.11 -> 6.07 s (-0.7 \%)}\td{-1.1 \%}}
\tr{\td{Std}\td{11.36, 11.16, 11.19 / 170.5 / 372}\td{11.10, 11.13, 11.11 / 169.1 / 372}\td{11.19 -> 11.11 s (-0.7 \%)}\td{-0.8 \%}}
}

\p{(8 / 11 / 164 / 203 units of these corpora are declined by the machine under the eager-reduction rule of the main tree and checked by the reference engine inside the same process; their cost is in both columns.) Lower on all four, none raised: \strong{KEEP \code{\verb~|k2~} and \code{\verb~|m3a~}} in this form. The Init question of batch 3 is gone with the arming (worker CPU 5.28, 5.19, 5.27 against 5.24, 5.24, 5.20 s). reachability stands at 1.4 - 1.5 s CPU (target 4 s; gruszka 3.97 s, nano-lean 2.08 s on this host); most of that is M7's inlined trees, the rules add the last 5 \%.}

\p{So the rules now serve what the trees do not: structural recursion through \code{\verb~|brecOn~} (\code{\verb~|_f~} auxiliaries), projection functions, wrappers. Gates of the version of 16:26Z (\code{\verb~|work/m3/diff-*-r-*.txt~}): K2 stress with \code{\verb~|code,casetrees,k2,m3a~} on tutorial + bugs + other + corner-cases + init-prelude 3,101 / 3,102 agree; reachability 4,216 / 4,224 and the Cedar slice 8,053 / 8,064 agree under \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,probes,code,casetrees,k2,m3a~} and under stress; 0 differences everywhere. The declines (1 / 8 / 11; 164 on Init and 203 on Std in the run of the 16:06Z version, 57,774 / 57,938 and 99,893 / 100,096 agree) are not K2's: \code{\verb~|UNSUPPORTED_INPUT (E_LIMIT): eager reduction (an argument 'eagerReduce _ _')~}, the rule of the main tree since about 15:20Z that hands such declarations to the reference engine. The same version on Init 57,774 / 57,938, Std 99,893 / 100,096, all 230 under the full switch set and under stress 15,839 / 15,845 (1 \code{\verb~|loop-unfolded-once~} E_MEM + 5 eager-reduction declines): 0 differences.}

\p{The numbers below are those of the first published version (15:05Z, before the trees were inlined and before the arming); they show what a rule saves where no better rule exists.}

\p{On reachability 0.92 M of the WHNF loop's unfoldings fire a rule (hit rate 97 \%); a node costs about 25 ticks to derive (74 - 148 nodes in each of the three heavy declarations, 0.05 \% of their ticks). The lazy-delta path (most of a \code{\verb~|decide~} proof's top-level chain) takes no rule, which bounds the gain there; \code{\verb~|magma-list-deep-n36~} is the shape the rules are for (\code{\verb~|List.get!Internal._f~} through \code{\verb~|brecOn~}: one firing per element instead of 4 unfoldings, 2 recursor steps and the closures of a matcher's alternatives): nano-lean's 10x there is reproduced. Gates (published code, \code{\verb~|work/m3/diff-*-h-*.txt~}, statistics \code{\verb~|work/m3/tmp/diffstats-*-h-*.json~}): \code{\verb~|code,casetrees,k2,m3a~} and \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,probes,code,casetrees,k2,m3a~}: the four corpora, all units agree, 0 differences, 0 declines (rules fired 23 k / 916 k / 54 k / 67 k and 24 k / 921 k / 148 k / 216 k times); STRESS mode (\code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.k2Hot=1 -Drlvm.machine.k2Share=0~}: a rule at the first unfolding, no cap): tutorial + bugs + other + corner-cases + init-prelude 3,102 units, reachability 4,224 (977 k firings), Cedar slice 8,064 (107 k firings): all agree, 0 differences, 0 declines; all 230 with \code{\verb~|code,casetrees,k2,m3a~}: 15,844 / 15,845 agree, 1 decline (\code{\verb~|loop-unfolded-once~}, as v0). Two defects of the first version, both found by the stress run before anything was published: a rule for a binary Nat function (its leaf was the application itself: the WHNF loop did not end; now no rule for them and no leaf equal to its application), and rules retired while they waited for the derivation allowance.}
}

\subtree{
\title{W3. Direct recursor rules (priority 4; D18): behind \code{\verb~|m3a~}}

\p{\code{\verb~|perf/unfold-before-literal~}, \code{\verb~|code,casetrees,k2~} (JVM launcher, counters): ticks 33.06 M -> 28.34 M, block activations 3.15 M -> 9.6 k, APPLY 6.29 M -> 4.72 M, records unchanged (14.17 M). The records stay because the minor premises of \code{\verb~|g~} are walked: \code{\verb~|g~} is unfolded three times and BODY(g) is elaborated at the 10th request; with \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.elabAt=1~} the same run makes 7.88 M records and EVAL falls from 4.72 M calls to 297 (user time 7.9 s -> 4.1 s on the JVM): request to M7 (requests.log 15:06Z).}
}

\subtree{
\title{W4. Deep evaluation (priority 3): measured, a request to M6, nothing of mine changed}

\p{Frames on reachability are host recursion beyond the bound, not a pattern of the reduction family: with \code{\verb~|k2,m3a~} D = 128 writes 149,475 frames (1.5 \% of the call events), D = 512 63,672, D = 2048 2,278 (0.02 \%, the 0.1 \% bound of H12 holds), D = 8192 none; ticks and call events are identical under all four. The derived rules alone take the frames from 348,827 to 130 k - 150 k (fewer nested judgments per step). The \code{\verb~|perf/~} literal loops are 2^19 deep by construction (\code{\verb~|g n a = ih (ih a)~}: the nesting of the delayed arguments); their 3.1 M frames do not depend on D (measured 128 / 2048 / 32768). CPU on the host: 3.02 / 2.84 / 2.96 / 2.77 s for D = 128 / 512 / 2048 / 8192 (one run each, loaded host: no difference established).}
}

\subtree{
\title{Rejected or not kept}

\ul{
\li{K2 with the allowance test at 256 ticks and allowance misses counted against a rule: rules were retired before their first node could be derived (reachability: 675 k of 686 k unfoldings met a retired head, 3 k firings); replaced by the form above before publication.}
}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{Observations for other packages}

\ul{
\li{A value ref below 2 (\code{\verb~|NONE~}, \code{\verb~|HOLE~}) reaching WHNF / CORE is \code{\verb~|fault(E_HOLE)~} / \code{\verb~|fault(E_INTERNAL)~}.}
\li{\code{\verb~|NatRed.natValue(m, handle)~} turns a result handle of \code{\verb~|rlvm.nat~} into a value or the \code{\verb~|E_NATSIZE~} abort; \code{\verb~|NatRed.litExt(m, v)~} is \code{\verb~|lit_ext~}; \code{\verb~|NatRed.boolConst(m, b)~}; \code{\verb~|NatRed.guard(m, which)~}.}
\li{\code{\verb~|Reduce.pushSpine(m, neu)~} / \code{\verb~|copyArgs~} copy a spine to scratch for an \code{\verb~|APPLY~}.}
}
}
